{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"question\":{\"text\":\"Should pressing a key before the start signal invalidate that round?\",\"decision\":\"This defines what happens when a player presses or holds a key early; five rounds and no persistent score history are otherwise sufficient to make a practical recommendation.\"},\"owner_view\":\"A browser file opened before the picnic can run this game offline. It can play five short rounds, wait a random time, show a clear signal, and award the round to the first player who presses their key afterward. The game should check that a key was released before the signal, so holding it early cannot win. Decide whether any early press should invalidate the round or simply be ignored. A custom one-file game would not need hosting or accounts; someone would keep the file and handle changes or recovery. A suitable existing offline game or a manual countdown are alternatives. Cost is unknown if you ask someone to create the file.\",\"developer_view\":{\"disposition\":\"needs_answer\",\"goal\":\"Choose a simple offline way for two adults at a picnic table to play five short keyboard reaction rounds on one laptop.\",\"users\":[\"Two adults sharing one laptop keyboard.\"],\"requirements\":[\"Use different keys for the two players.\",\"Wait a random interval and show a clear visual start signal each round.\",\"Award each round to the first valid keypress after the signal.\",\"Prevent a player from winning by holding a key before the signal, for example by requiring keys to be released at the start signal.\",\"Provide five short rounds and a simple way to start or reset play.\"],\"constraints\":[\"A browser is available and can open a file beforehand.\",\"Internet may not be available at the picnic.\",\"Laptop operating system is unknown.\",\"No persistent scores or records have been requested.\"],\"data_access\":[\"Play can take place locally in the browser; no accounts, personal data, network connection, or hosting are needed for the described use.\"],\"risk\":{\"level\":\"low\",\"reasons\":[\"Casual local play with no sensitive data described.\",\"False-start behavior remains undecided and affects the game rules.\"]},\"recommendation\":{\"summary\":\"Use a local browser file if no suitable offline game already fits; prepare and open it before the picnic. Require both keys to be released at the start signal so an early held key cannot win.\",\"rationale\":[\"A browser file matches the owner's offline setup.\",\"Local play avoids accounts, hosting, and service costs.\",\"A small game can support the specified two-key, random-signal, five-round flow.\"],\"alternatives\":[\"Use a spoken countdown and play manually with no software.\",\"Use an existing offline game if it supports two distinct keys and the required rules.\",\"Consider a small custom local game if an existing option does not fit; creation cost and maintenance effort are unknown.\"]},\"assumptions\":[\"The keyboard can register both players' selected keys.\",\"No score history beyond the five rounds is needed.\",\"Requiring keys to be released at the signal addresses holding a key early; whether any early press invalidates the round is still undecided.\"],\"open_questions\":[\"Should any keypress before the signal invalidate that round, or should it be ignored while requiring keys to be released before the signal?\"],\"acceptance_criteria\":[\"Opens from a file in the available browser and works without internet.\",\"Supports two distinct player keys on one keyboard.\",\"Starts each round after a random delay and clearly signals when pressing is allowed.\",\"Does not let a key held before the signal win; the agreed early-press rule is followed.\",\"Runs five short rounds and makes restarting straightforward.\",\"The owner understands the file's location, how to open it, likely costs, and who will maintain or recover it.\"],\"owner_responsibilities\":[\"Choose whether early presses invalidate the round or are ignored, while preventing held keys from winning.\",\"Keep the game file accessible and open it before play if using a custom file.\",\"Arrange any future changes or file recovery if needed.\"]}}"}}
