eplace or retrieve copies as leadership changes.\",\"Consider a small managed custom solution only if available services cannot meet the access and update needs.\"]},\"assumptions\":[\"The organizer can manage who is appointed as a section leader.\",\"No particular file or contacts service has yet been confirmed.\"],\"open_questions\":[\"What tools does the orchestra already use for shared files or contacts?\",\"Who will maintain the list's accuracy, and what details should it contain?\",\"How promptly must access be removed when a leader rotates out?\"],\"acceptance_criteria\":[\"Only the organizer and currently appointed section leaders can access the complete list.\",\"Current leaders can read it in a phone browser.\",\"The organizer can update access when leaders change without administering a server.\"],\"owner_responsibilities\":[\"Identify the existing file or contacts tools available to the orchestra.\",\"Choose a person to maintain the list and its accuracy.\",\"Update access when section leaders are appointed or leave.\"]}}"}, {"role": "owner", "text": "I do not know."}, {"role": "assistant", "text": "{\"question\":{\"text\":\"Does the orchestra already use a shared file or contacts service, or should the recommendation assume it has none?\",\"decision\":\"This determines whether to recommend configuring a familiar service or first comparing available options; you said you do not know, so I will preserve that uncertainty rather than assume either answer.\"},\"owner_view\":\"A service with named-user access may meet your needs: only the organizer and current section leaders would see the list, and leaders could read it in phone browsers. You do not know what tools the orchestra already uses, so I can’t yet recommend a specific service. No server administration or custom app is established as necessary. The organizer would need to keep the list accurate and update access as leaders change.\",\"developer_view\":{\"disposition\":\"needs_answer\",\"goal\":\"Pro