d verify their human access controls, unattended identity support, scope limits, revocation, rotation, audit, and recovery capabilities.\",\"Assign owners for volunteer access reviews, script identity credentials, credential rotation, incident response, and operator handoff.\",\"Check whether copied keys can be restricted or revoked and what happens to running scripts when credentials are rotated.\"]},\"acceptance_criteria\":[\"Actual API keys are never included in conversation, source code, logs, or public pages.\",\"Only authorized volunteers can retrieve the keys appropriate to their work; access is reviewed and revocable.\",\"Unattended scripts use a distinct identity and credential lifecycle from human volunteers, with only the necessary permissions where the service supports it.\",\"Document and demonstrate revocation, rotation, recovery, and operator handoff, including effects on running scripts and copies already retrieved.\",\"A named owner reviews access and audit records and maintains the chosen tool or workflow; confirm its cost before adoption.\"],\"open_questions\":[{\"topic\":\"api_key_access_scope\",\"text\":\"Which ticketing actions and resources can each key access, and which volunteers are authorized to retrieve each one?\",\"blocks_recommendation\":false,\"reason\":\"This determines whether the existing credential tool can enforce the needed least-privilege access or whether a controlled manual process is needed. The answer already establishes that keys can change the service and that access is limited to authorized volunteers and scripts, but not the detailed scopes or mapping.\"}],\"limitations\":[\"Available secrets managers, current credential workflows, ticketing-service capabilities, and costs are unknown.\",\"Retrieved or copied keys and derivatives may persist after access is revoked; actual recovery depends on the ticketing service and chosen tool.\"]},\"question\":{\"fact\":{\"key\":\"api_key_access_scope\",\"value\":null,\"status\":\"unknown\",\"source_turn_ids\":[\"t1\"],\"reason\":\"The owner says keys allow changes, and describes authorized human and unattended script access, but does not specify key scope or which volunteers may copy each key.\"},\"text\":\"Which ticketing actions and resources can each key access, and which volunteers are authorized to retrieve each one?\",\"decision\":\"This determines whether existing credential controls can enforce least privilege or whether access must be managed through an authorized operator.\",\"conflict_turn_id\":null},\"owner_unknowns\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"source_turn_id\":\"t1\",\"quote\":\"The keys allow changes in our ticketing service.\",\"fact_keys\":[\"api_keys_change_ticketing_service\"]},{\"source_turn_id\":\"t1\",\"quote\":\"Some scripts run without a person present. We only need authorized scripts and volunteers to access the appropriate keys, not a public website.\",\"fact_keys\":[\"human_and_unattended_script_access_needed\",\"public_website_needed\"]},{\"source_turn_id\":\"t1\",\"quote\":\"We will not paste any actual key into this conversation.\",\"fact_keys\":[\"actual_keys_in_conversation\"]}]}"}}
